        "summary": "The create side has had an identity seam since 3.11.0 (FLOW_PR_CREATE_CMD) but the merge side had none - a repo whose branch protection excludes the tick's human identity simply could not merge (#337). A PR behind its base was caught up by local rebase + force-push, which rewrites every commit SHA (the CAUSE of #302's orphaned evidence, previously only detected) and, on repos that dismiss stale approvals on push, voids the approval the merge was waiting for - deterministic non-convergence (#342). And the post-merge tail persisted the spec close by pushing to the base FIRST, so on a PR-only base the refused push skipped release-follow AND the tracker touchpoint - the board stuck at In Review after a real merge, the exact outcome land.merged exists to prevent (#345). All three from @sn-furali; every structural claim verified against the file.",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "Three ways land could not finish what it started"
