        "summary": "The §3.5 merge call runs through MERGE_CMD (default gh pr merge), unquoted #277-shape expansion, with a STABLE inline contract: fixed argument order; exit 0 = merged; stderr proxied VERBATIM (the RESOLVING/BLOCKED classification reads gh's head-mismatch stderr text - a wrapper that eats it turns benign races into BLOCKED); never --auto or merge-queue (the merge-license boundary binds the interposed command); merge-call-only scope (every other gh call stays on the session identity); the --delete-branch second-permission note. Env-only, deliberately never a land.* key - fn-188's own trust guard proved config-sourced command strings are PR-author-influenceable and session env is not.",
