        "summary": "BEHIND and DIRTY both plan catch-up: one gh pr update-branch call (merge-based; GitHub's conflict refusal IS the BLOCKED verdict - land still never hand-resolves a hunk), ledger head sourced from the API, RESOLVING on success. No local checkout, no git rebase, no --force-with-lease anywhere in the skill - commit SHAs survive, so the #302 orphaned-evidence cause is removed for every repo, and land loses its single most dangerous capability. No land.catchUp key: land always squash-merges, so branch-local linearity is invisible after merge - a key would buy a forever five-host contract for an unobservable property. The §2.6/§2.7 evaluation order under reviewSignal: approve is stated where the agent had to guess: the stale-approval detector IS reachable (only §2.1 stops the fall-through) and the durable label is what breaks the dismissal loop.",
