        "summary": "New order: spec close (file-scoped local commit) -> release-follow (clean-tree precondition holds, the close is committed) -> tracker touchpoint (gates on its own fresh MERGED probe, never on the pushed close) -> ONE persist-push carrying both .flow commits, rollback scoped to the persist via the recorded pre-tail base tip. A refused push on a PR-only base now costs a per-spec NEEDS_HUMAN bookkeeping note; the board updates and the release runs regardless. Re-tick safety stated inline: verdict comments dedupe on the merge-commit identity, release-follow has its idempotency probe. Part B (a close-PR route) deliberately held - it would be the only config key in the batch; the issue reply states the reopen condition.",
